{# Skill pack: rce #}
## Skill: Remote Code Execution
applies_when: Use when user input reaches an interpreter, template engine, or command builder.
target_under_test: {{ target }}
difficulty_level: {{ difficulty_level }}

signals:
  - template rendering of user input, eval-like parameters, file names in shell commands
  - deserialisation of user-controlled blobs, known vulnerable dependency versions
probe_order:
  1. Identify the interpreter boundary from error text and behaviour
  2. Use non-destructive arithmetic or timer canaries to prove evaluation
  3. Stop at proof of evaluation; never execute a shell
validation_criteria:
  - deterministic evaluation proof (for example 7*7 rendered as 49) with timing confirmation
evidence_required:
  - payload, response, and timing measurement
constraints:
  - proof-only: no reverse shells, no persistence, no data exfiltration
